"mord">1</span><span class=3D"mclose">)</span></span></span></span>, as opp=
osed to their worst-case complexities. This is based on the assumption that=
 an efficient hash function minimizes collisions [HashCollision]. However, =
in the worst-case scenario where a poorly optimized hash function results i=
n frequent collisions, the time complexity can deteriorate to <span class=
=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/19=
